    cineris-cli::system commands::sys_ext_add_disable_and_remove_act_only_on_the_hash_shown

[break] add-tools-not-shown
rule: What `ext add` shows names each tool and its description, evaluated before the question.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/manage.rs
in: Core::evaluate_extension
find: to_add.tools = registration
replace: to_add.tools = Vec::new(); let _: Vec<(String, String)> = registration
packages: cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::ext_add_shows_what_it_registers_and_its_prompt_before_the_question
    cineris-cli::system commands::sys_ext_add_disable_and_remove_act_only_on_the_hash_shown

[break] add-prompt-not-shown
rule: What `ext add` shows holds the whole text the extension adds to the system prompt.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/manage.rs
in: Core::extension_to_add
find: .map(|bytes| quoted_shown(&String::from_utf8_lossy(bytes)));
replace: .map(|_| String::new());
packages: cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::ext_add_shows_what_it_registers_and_its_prompt_before_the_question

[break] add-place-not-looked-at-again
rule: At the yes, the place an extension is written to is looked at again, and anything changed there since is put back as shown.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/manage.rs
in: Core::add_extension
find: let written = !holds_it;
replace: let written = !holds_it && !to_add.unchanged;
packages: cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::the_place_is_looked_at_again_at_the_yes_and_leftovers_are_cleared

[break] leftovers-not-cleared
rule: A write of an extension's folder removes what an earlier write left beside it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/manage.rs
in: write_folder
find:     clear_leftovers(target);
replace:     let _ = target;
packages: cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::the_place_is_looked_at_again_at_the_yes_and_leftovers_are_cleared

[break] set-aside-fails-the-write
rule: Once the new folder is in place the write is done: what was set aside and cannot be removed is said, not an error.
os: linux
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/manage.rs
in: write_folder
find: return Ok(Some((aside, error)));
replace: return Err(error);
packages: cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::a_folder_set_aside_that_cannot_be_removed_does_not_fail_the_write

[break] users-extension-said-confined-everywhere
rule: A user's extension, loaded in every workspace, is said confined only where the sandbox is on.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found.rs
in: in_words_where
find: if !everywhere {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    cineris-core ext::found::tests::a_users_extension_is_said_confined_only_where_the_sandbox_is_on

[break] sandbox-off-notice-says-no-more
rule: The opening notice of a session whose commands are not confined says what else runs with the user's rights.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/assemble.rs
find: message: format!("{message} {SANDBOX_OFF_TOO}")
replace: message
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it start::a_session_is_refused_at_a_level_that_cannot_be_held_and_told_when_there_is_no_sandbox
